Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: The Scale Drops After the String Dies
- Story & Context: At 118 BPM, Soa opens with a four-note valiha cell: two bright plucks, one muted octave, then a final open fifth. She kills the fifth quickly against the bamboo tube, leaving only a short hollow body resonance. Nkosinathi leaves the next half-beat completely empty before dropping one kick and a short root sub. Lala answers only during HOLLOW with one damped Rhodes minor seventh. Sibusiso replaces every third expected kick with a deep hand-drum hit. Inès enters after the longest VOID with a breath-heavy low fundamental, cut off before the next sub block. At the midpoint, the electronic low end disappears for eight bars while the Vacancy Pressure Cycle continues acoustically. When the sub returns, no fill announces it.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Low-angle view of a rusted freight scale beside a bamboo valiha, one string visibly damped against the tube, a waveform showing bright attack collapsing into hollow resonance and then a blank gap before a single heavy low-frequency block. Sparse spoken fragments limited to “string dies,” “scale drops,” “leave the gap,” and “weight returns.”

Track 2: Rain Gauge Zero, Floor Still Shaking
- Story & Context: At 122 BPM, Nkosinathi programs the EP’s hardest kick pattern but removes sub from half the impacts. Soa alternates muted ghost plucks and open dyads, making some machine kicks feel enormous and others strangely weightless. Lala plays prepared Rhodes octaves only after sub-less kicks. Sibusiso uses one low drum as a false bass cue, making the listener expect sub that never arrives. Inès contributes short contrabass-clarinet bursts after selected silences, creating pressure through air rather than electronics. In the final minute, every kick remains but the sub appears only once every four bars, increasing expectation instead of density.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Old rain gauge reading zero beside a wet concrete floor with faint concentric vibration lines, bamboo strings and one black subwoofer cone in shallow focus. Spoken fragments limited to “zero rain,” “floor still moves,” “kick without weight,” and “wait four bars.”

Track 3: Rattan Bay Holds the Empty Measure
- Story & Context: The closer runs at 114 BPM and begins with almost no drum machine. Soa plays widely spaced low valiha dyads, each followed by a long HOLLOW decay and a full-beat VOID. Lala uses single prepared Rhodes notes with no sustain pedal. Sibusiso contributes one hand-drum impact every eight beats. Inès holds a low contrabass-clarinet pitch through two VOID states, then abruptly cuts it so the third VOID is truly empty. Nkosinathi introduces sub only in the second half, one short block every four bars. The final section removes all electronics. Soa plucks one low string, mutes it, and leaves the last measure completely silent before the recording ends.
